{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":788},{"base":"H0444","lemma":"אָלַח","tr":"a·lach","gloss":"to corrupt","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H5036","lemma":"נָבָל","tr":"na·val","gloss":"foolish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H8259","lemma":"שָׁקַף","tr":"sha·qaph","gloss":"to look","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H8581","lemma":"תַּעָב","tr":"ta·av","gloss":"to abhor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H5949","lemma":"עֲלִילָה","tr":"a·li·lah","gloss":"wantonness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H7919","lemma":"שָׂכַל","tr":"sa·khal","gloss":"be prudent","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":62},{"base":"H3426","lemma":"יֵשׁ","tr":"yesh","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":138},{"base":"H3162","lemma":"יַ֫חַד","tr":"ya·chad","gloss":"unitedness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":141}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":128,"source":"both","text":"As it is written: “There is no one righteous, not even one.","from":3},{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":128,"source":"openbible","text":"All have turned away, they have together become worthless; there is no one who does good, not even one.”","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":53,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":95,"source":"both","text":"We all like sheep have gone astray, each one has turned to his own way; and the LORD has laid upon Him the iniquity of us all.","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":64,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":88,"source":"both","text":"Each of us has become like something unclean, and all our righteous acts are like filthy rags; we all wither like a leaf, and our iniquities carry us away like the wind.","from":3},{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":64,"source":"both","text":"for all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God,","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":59,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":51,"source":"openbible","text":"rebelling and denying the LORD, turning away from our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering lies from the heart.","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":59,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":51,"source":"openbible","text":"Truth is missing, and whoever turns from evil becomes prey. The LORD looked and was displeased that there was no justice.","from":3},{"book":"ISA","chapter":59,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":50,"source":"openbible","text":"Their feet run to evil; they are swift to shed innocent blood. Their thoughts are sinful thoughts; ruin and destruction lie in their wake.","from":3}],"notes":[{"id":"ps-14-1-none-righteous","title":"There is no one righteous","kind":"quotation"}],"groups":[]},"4-6":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0398","lemma":"אָכַל","tr":"a·khal","gloss":"to eat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":810},{"base":"H4268","lemma":"מַחְסֶּה","tr":"ma·cha·seh","gloss":"refuge","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H6342","lemma":"פָּחַד","tr":"pa·chad","gloss":"to dread","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25},{"base":"H6343","lemma":"פַּ֫חַד","tr":"pa·chad","gloss":"dread","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":49},{"base":"H6466","lemma":"פָּעַל","tr":"pa·al","gloss":"to work","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":57},{"base":"H6041","lemma":"עָנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"afflicted","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":74},{"base":"H0205","lemma":"אָ֫וֶן","tr":"a·ven","gloss":"evil: wickedness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":77},{"base":"H6098","lemma":"עֵצָה","tr":"e·tsah","gloss":"counsel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":89},{"base":"H0954","lemma":"בּוֹשׁ","tr":"bush","gloss":"be ashamed","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":127},{"base":"H1755","lemma":"דּוֹר","tr":"dor","gloss":"generation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":167}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":79,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Pour out Your wrath on the nations that do not acknowledge You, on the kingdoms that refuse to call on Your name,","from":4},{"book":"JER","chapter":10,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Pour out Your wrath on the nations that do not acknowledge You, and on the families that do not call on Your name. For they have devoured Jacob; they have consumed him and finished him off; they have devastated his homeland.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":82,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"They do not know or understand; they wander in the darkness; all the foundations of the earth are shaken.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":112,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"His descendants will be mighty in the land; the generation of the upright will be blessed.","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":64,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"No one calls on Your name or strives to take hold of You. For You have hidden Your face from us and delivered us into the hand of our iniquity.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":73,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"If I had said, “I will speak this way,” then I would have betrayed Your children.","from":5},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Furthermore, since they did not see fit to acknowledge God, He gave them up to a depraved mind, to do what ought not to be done.","from":4},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and terror and dread will fall on them. By the power of Your arm they will be as still as a stone until Your people pass by, O LORD, until the people You have bought pass by.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-7":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"H7622","lemma":"שְׁבִית","tr":"she·vut","gloss":"captivity","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":32},{"base":"H1523","lemma":"גִּיל","tr":"gil","gloss":"to rejoice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":45},{"base":"H3444","lemma":"יְשׁוּעָה","tr":"ye·shu·ah","gloss":"salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":78},{"base":"H6726","lemma":"צִיּוֹן","tr":"tsiy·yon","gloss":"Zion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":154},{"base":"H8055","lemma":"שָׂמַח","tr":"sa·mach","gloss":"to rejoice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":155},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":350},{"base":"H4310","lemma":"מִי","tr":"mi","gloss":"who?","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":423},{"base":"H7725","lemma":"שׁוּב","tr":"shuv","gloss":"to return: return","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":1057}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":53,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come from Zion! When God restores His captive people, let Jacob rejoice, let Israel be glad!","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}